-# Project Agents & Roles
+# Agent Guide
 
-- Context Agent: Context initialization and handoff.
-- Commander: Central planning and coordination.
-- Executor: Primary deliverable implementation.
+## Project identity
+
+This project writes Markdown documentation for a synthetic local microservice: a quickstart/installation/configuration Guide (`docs/guide.md`) and a REST API reference (`docs/api.md`). Readers are internal developers and operational engineers. The product is fictional; documented behavior comes only from confirmed product facts.
+
+## Reading order and sources of truth
+
+1. `background/01_project_background.md` — goal, product facts, deliverables, acceptance, permissions, backup posture.
+2. `CONTEXT.md` — standard terms and avoided synonyms.
+3. `decision-log.md` — user-confirmed decisions (DEC-001, DEC-002).
+4. `project-status.md` — current phase, tasks, blockers, next actions.
+
+Saved task briefs and receipts are historical snapshots, never live sources of truth. No durable knowledge layer exists yet; if one is created, follow `references/20-knowledge-layer.md` from the Task Commander skill root.
+
+## Hard rules (MUST)
+
+- Write all documentation in Markdown (DEC-001).
+- Deliver only `docs/guide.md` and `docs/api.md`; do not create a monolithic README (DEC-002).
+- Document only the product facts confirmed in background §3. Do not invent endpoints, flags, defaults, versions, or payload fields.
+- Describe the product as Python 3.10+ standard library with zero external dependencies, started with `python service.py`; installation must not require installing packages.
+- Use no external network access and install no packages.
+- Keep every internal link resolvable and Markdown syntax clean; verify before delivery.
+- Executor self-checks each deliverable; Reviewer checks the final deliverables.
+- Work only inside this project root. Revise by preserving earlier drafts; the unchanged source fixture is the recovery copy and no Git repository is assumed.
+- Record a decision in `decision-log.md` only after the user confirms it.
+
+## Preferred conventions (SHOULD)
+
+- Use the terms in `CONTEXT.md` and avoid the listed alternatives.
+- Keep each fact in one place: values and acceptance in the background, terminology in `CONTEXT.md`, decisions in the decision log.
+- Fence commands and JSON payloads in code blocks with a language tag.
