 # Project Context
 
-- Project: Synthetic Microservice Documentation
-- Current Phase: Context Building
-- Status: All core facts, deliverables, policies, and decisions are established and confirmed with the user. Zero pending items. Ready for Commander handoff.
+Sole source of truth for standard terms, avoided terms, and domain relations. Product facts, scope, and policies live in `background/01_project_background.md`.
+
+## Terms
+
+| Term | Definition | Avoid |
+|---|---|---|
+| Service | The local microservice that this project documents, started with `python service.py`. | app, server, backend |
+| Guide | The `docs/guide.md` deliverable: installation, startup, and configuration content. | README, manual, quickstart doc |
+| API reference | The `docs/api.md` deliverable: the endpoint reference. | API docs, Swagger, spec |
+| Health endpoint | `GET /health`; reports whether the Service is alive. | healthcheck route, ping endpoint |
+| Status endpoint | `GET /status`; reports the Service's uptime and version. | metrics endpoint, info endpoint |
+| Uptime | Whole seconds the Service has been running; an integer field of the status response. | runtime, lifetime, duration |
+| Version | The Service release identifier; a string field of the status response. | build number, release tag |
+| Configuration flag | An environment variable that changes Service runtime behavior. | option, setting, config key |
+| `PORT` | Configuration flag for the Service's listening port. | port number, listen port |
+| `LOG_LEVEL` | Configuration flag for logging verbosity. | log mode, verbosity setting |
+| Deliverable | A document in the confirmed delivery scope of this project. | artifact, output |
+
+## Domain relations
+
+- The Service exposes the Health endpoint and the Status endpoint.
+- Configuration flags configure the Service; `PORT` and `LOG_LEVEL` are the confirmed flags.
+- The Guide owns installation, startup, and configuration language; the API reference owns endpoint language.
+- The Status endpoint reports Uptime and Version; the Health endpoint reports only liveness.
